{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 asserts a substantive contradiction between 07c3398912d4 and SRC_004's determinism: greedy enumeration order changes which undecided nodes are labelled suspended. But the stated refutation condition (two enumeration orders yielding identical suspend_reason sets) fails to isolate the contradiction, because identical suspend_reason sets can still arise from different individual labels that merely cancel out over the whole set. A correct refutation would demand identical per-node suspend_reason under both orders; requiring only set equality is compatible with exactly the nondeterminism the relation claims to expose, leaving the contradiction unsupported.","target":"13f3a6d2359a807b7307eaf84a98e901ff6267cedd96941d71f532c345a5bf3c"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_002 claims integration of SRC_006's carriage closure with SRC_011's inner/outer split by materializing every attacker-of-validity_node as an attacker of the carriage edge before the inner pass. But this ordering is incompatible with the inner labelling feeding outer acceptance: an attacker whose validity node is not yet accepted (or is undecided) at inner-fixpoint time cannot be consistently materialized as a live carriage attacker without anticipating the outer pass. The refutation condition (an outer-only attacker needed for carriage survival) is therefore not an edge case but the normal feedback the integration ignores, so the relation fails by incoherent phase ordering.","target":"2f56123fcafff1615e4e1e38de56f4118d0fccd69c5b73f10bfea487b41a75df"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_003 claims shared mechanism with SRC_010 via first-class warrant-carrying attack nodes with unchanged grounded fixpoint, and offers a refutation only for double-counting (two accepted attackers with one 'out'). But the deeper compatibility failure is unaddressed: promoting an edge into a node can invert the grounding of the original target when the warrant node's own attackers form a grounding path that the edge-only semantics never considered. Because the refutation omits this label-inversion pathway, the shared-mechanism claim is not actually protected by the stated counterexample guard.","target":"63f5865aa585da7cc02cf774d6bc22a8979a00ac39c77adbdae0a1364523dc56"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_004 frames the dependence on SRC_011 as a clean two-level split: inner validity governs force, outer acceptance governs activation, and the refutation targets an outer-accepted argument attacking a warrant. But a warrant node can also be attacked by an argument that is itself only accepted because of the warrant's current 'out' status — a self-referential loop spanning both levels that the refutation's condition (outer-accepted attacker changing inner) mischaracterizes as merely outer-only. Since the actual feedback can originate at the inner level through a warrant-dependent path, the stated refutation does not catch the two-pass defect it claims to.","target":"dd9740367211b37e73b940e16e5974f326223e816d17fbd1b98c788eaef30174"}]}